  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal obligations to New York are $191M for FY2027 to date. The federal government recorded 8,812 awards in the state, with an average award size of $21.6K. Obligations are down 98.3% year over year compared with prior fiscal years, following a multi-year decline from $29.4B in FY22 through $11.4B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer this fiscal year, obligating $157M. The Department of Justice and the General Services Administration follow with $14.3M and $13.5M in obligations respectively. Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $33.7M. WELCH ALLYN, INC. is the largest vendor by obligations at $30.1M. This snapshot covers partial, fiscal year to date totals and shows a concentrated set of buyers and vendors responsible for the bulk of current-year spending.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in New York this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs accounts for the largest share with $157M in obligations. The top three agencies together are the Department of Veterans Affairs, the Department of Justice, and the General Services Administration, with $157M, $14.3M, and $13.5M respectively. The top industries include Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing at $33.7M and Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing at $21.4M. The top vendors include WELCH ALLYN, INC. and SIEMENS HEALTHCARE DIAGNOSTICS INC., with $30.1M and $16.1M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations for FY27 to date are $191M, compared with $11.4B in FY26 and $29.4B in FY22. Obligations trended downward from FY22 through FY26 before arriving at the current-year total. The award count for FY27 to date is 8,812 with an average award size of $21.6K. The year over year change is down 98.3%."
      }
    ]
  },
